---
// Mirror the in-app privacy audit without inventing a competitor traffic
// estimate. The number is explicitly scoped to inference during a local-mode
// turn; downloads, update checks, and enabled remote tiers are separate.
---

<section id="pace-local-turn-proof" aria-label="Local-turn network audit and founder note" class="px-6 pt-32 pb-16 border-t border-[var(--color-border-subtle)] mt-20">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <!-- ───── Local-turn privacy status ───── -->
    <div class="mb-28 md:mb-36">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] gap-10 md:gap-20 items-end">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-5">
            Local-turn network audit
          </p>
          <h2 class="pace-display text-4xl md:text-6xl text-white">
            The privacy claim is a <em>number inside the app.</em>
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="md:border-l md:border-[var(--color-border-subtle)] md:pl-12">
          <p class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-4">
            Voice · screen · planner · speech-out
          </p>
          <div
            class="pace-display text-[var(--color-positive)] tabular-nums"
            style="font-size: clamp(6rem, 16vw, 11rem); line-height: 0.85;"
          >
            0
            <span class="text-2xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">bytes</span>
          </div>
          <p class="pace-margin-note text-sm mt-3">
            For a local-mode turn. Model downloads, Sparkle update checks, and
            any remote planner you explicitly enable are counted separately.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ───── Signed letter ───── -->
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto pace-prose mb-20">
      <p
        class="pace-margin-note text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-6 not-italic font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider"
      >
        A note from me
      </p>
      <p>
        I built Pace because every assistant I tried either lived in someone
        else's data center or couldn't actually <em>do</em> anything. I wanted
        Siri's reach with a local model's privacy and a real agent's hands.
        Nobody was making it, so I did.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you try it and the third turn feels worse than I promised, email
        me directly. I want to know where it failed and make the purchase
        terms clear before you pay. That's the whole quality bar.
      </p>
      <p class="pace-display text-2xl text-white mt-8 not-italic">
        — <em>Sarthak</em>
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-1">
        <a href="mailto:hi@sarthakagrawal.dev" class="underline hover:text-white"
          >hi@sarthakagrawal.dev</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
